<article class="env-corollary" id="B7A1FF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B7A1FF">Corollary <span data-tag="B7A1FF">4.2.1.8</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category containing vertices $x$ and $y$. The maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(x,y) \rightarrow \Hom _{\calC }(x,y) \leftarrow \Hom ^{\lft }_{\calC }(x,y) \]
</div>
  <p> are homotopy equivalences of Kan complexes (see §<a href="/tag/887669" data-tag="887669">1.2.2</a> for an explanation of this notation). </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a href="/tag/ABFCF4" data-tag="ABFCF4">4.2.1.7</a> (the dual of Corollary <a href="/tag/ABFCF4" data-tag="ABFCF4">4.2.1.7</a>) to the case where $p$ is the inclusion $\{ x \}  \subseteq \calC $ (the inclusion $\{ y\}  \subseteq \calC $). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>